    "body": "## Summary\n\n- prevent the global `mla_up_proj` selective-recompute setting from being inherited by non-MLA VLM components\n- preserve `mla_up_proj` on MLA foundation models\n- emit the compatibility warning through `warn_rank_0` to avoid duplicate messages from every rank\n\n## Problem\n\nVLM parsing copies global training arguments to the foundation model, image encoder, and image projector. When an MLA foundation enables `mla_up_proj`, non-MLA vision components inherit the same entry and fail `TransformerConfig` validation with:\n\n```text\nmla_up_proj in recompute_modules is only supported with multi_latent_attention.\n```\n\nLoongForge already filters component-incompatible `a2a_*` recompute entries in this validation path. This change follows the same inline filtering pattern for the MLA-only entry without modifying the foundation configuration.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `ruff==0.9.10` passed for the changed Python file\n- Python 3.12 syntax checks passed\n- the equivalent fix was validated in a successful multi-node 32B VLM selective-recompute training run",
    "changed_files": 1,
